// Powder Cellar: the data-driven material and reaction tables as a chain of
// chemistry in the dark, each step started by the one before. Only the falling
// brand is scripted; every later step comes from the material table.
//
// A burning brand drops from a lantern onto a gunpowder trail. Gunpowder
// explodes at 200 C with radius 9, so the trail burns as a crackling line of
// tiny blasts along the floor, up the stone stair and along the shelf to two
// powder kegs. The acid carboy stands on the first keg, which blows it apart.
// Acid eats brick, stone, wood and metal into green acid_gas but not glass,
// which is why it was kept in glass (a glass sill also keeps it off the straw).
// It runs down the brick wall, eats the wooden shelf under it so its jars
// tumble, and pools on the floor eating pits. Burning debris lights oil spilled
// over straw in a floor sump; the fire creeps along it under the shelf,
// setting the hanging oil barrels alight one by one, until it reaches the drain
// mouth. Oil that catches fire burns as a liquid where it lies, so the sump
// and the barrels burn on by themselves. A second trail runs under the bedrock
// floor slab and up the far stair to the powder store. Its kegs set off the
// TNT beside them (150 C, radius 18): a blast sets off every charge it reaches,
// so the 144 cells of TNT go up together, merged into one large blast that
// flashes white through the whole cellar, throws a fireball and burning
// debris, and blows out the far corner.
//
// The light is the reactions' own: lamps and torches, sparks, burning oil and
// timber, and the acid's green glow.
[scene]
name = powder cellar
description = A brand drops on a powder trail in a dark vaulted cellar; the spark runs up the stair to the kegs, the blast frees a carboy of acid that eats the wall, a shelf and the floor, burning oil creeps along the straw to a second trail under the floor, and the powder store blows out the far corner.
size = 760 430
seed = 0xc0d5
ticks = 2160

